stream
BT /F2 16 Tf 54 723 Td (Halcyon Sensor Replacement Procedure) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 701 Td (Document ID: sup-hx-sensor-replacement-procedure | Revision: 3 | Effective: 2025-03-10 | Owner:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 688 Td (Customer Support Technical Services, Leeds) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 663 Td (1. Scope) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 641 Td (This procedure describes how to replace the gas sensors in Halcyon HX-200, HX-210 and HX-220) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 628 Td (portable gas detectors. It is intended for customer maintenance technicians who have completed) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 615 Td (Meridian Halcyon service training, and for Meridian field service engineers. Replacing sensors) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 602 Td (does not require the instrument to be returned under RMA.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 580 Td (Replacement sensors:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 558 Td (- HX-SNS-H2S-02: H2S sensor \(HX-200, HX-210, HX-220\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 545 Td (- HX-SNS-CO-03: CO sensor \(HX-210, HX-220\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 532 Td (- HX-SNS-LEL-04: catalytic LEL sensor \(HX-210, HX-220\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 519 Td (- HX-SNS-O2-01: O2 sensor \(HX-210, HX-220\)) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 503 Td (2. Safety and preparation) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 481 Td (- Work only in a safe \(non-hazardous\) area, on an antistatic mat, with the instrument) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 468 Td (   switched off.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 455 Td (- Wear an antistatic wrist strap.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 442 Td (- Have a new rear housing gasket \(HX-GSK-200, HX-GSK-210 or HX-GSK-220\) ready. The gasket) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 429 Td (   must be replaced every time the housing is opened for sensor replacement.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 416 Td (- Tools: Torx T10 driver \(T8 for the HX-200\), torque screwdriver adjustable from 0.2 to 1.0) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 403 Td (   N m, plastic spudger.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 390 Td (- Check the new sensor's date code. Do not fit a sensor that has been stored for more than 6) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 377 Td (   months from its date code.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 361 Td (3. Removing the rear housing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 339 Td (1. Remove the belt clip.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 326 Td (2. Undo the rear housing screws: four Torx T8 screws on the HX-200, six Torx T10 screws on) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 313 Td (   the HX-210, eight Torx T10 screws on the HX-220.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 300 Td (3. Lift the rear housing and disconnect the battery connector.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 287 Td (4. Remove and discard the old gasket.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 271 Td (4. Replacing the LEL sensor \(HX-SNS-LEL-04\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 249 Td (The LEL sensor is fitted only in the HX-210 and HX-220. Replace it when the instrument shows) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 236 Td (E-117 \(LEL sensor poisoned or bridge fault\), when the sensor life shown at Menu > Instrument >) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 223 Td (Service > Sensor Life is below 20%, or when E-104 recurs on the LEL channel after a correct) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 210 Td (calibration.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 188 Td (1. Locate the LEL sensor in the top-right position of the sensor board, marked "LEL".) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 175 Td (2. Remove the two Torx T6 screws holding the sensor retaining bracket.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 162 Td (3. Lift the sensor straight out of its socket using the spudger under the flange. Do not rock) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 149 Td (   it; the pins bend easily.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 136 Td (4. Inspect the socket for corrosion. Clean with a dry brush only; do not use solvent.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 123 Td (5. Insert the new HX-SNS-LEL-04 with the locating tab facing the display.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 110 Td (6. Refit the retaining bracket and tighten the two Torx T6 screws to 0.25 N m.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 97 Td (7. Reconnect the battery and refit the rear housing with a new gasket. Tighten the rear) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 84 Td (   housing screws to 0.45 N m in a diagonal pattern.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 71 Td (8. Switch on the instrument. It detects the new sensor and shows "NEW SENSOR". Confirm with) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 58 Td (   ON/OK.) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
