6 0 obj
<< /Length 2675 >>
stream
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 729 Td (9. Leave the instrument switched on in clean air for a warm-up period of 4 hours before) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 716 Td (   calibrating. The catalytic bead needs this time to stabilise; calibrating earlier gives a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 703 Td (   span that drifts by up to 10% LEL in the first day.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 690 Td (10. Perform a full calibration \(all channels\), following prod-hx210-calibration-procedure-v2) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 677 Td (   for the HX-210 or the HX-220 user manual for the HX-220.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 664 Td (11. Perform a bump test before returning the instrument to service.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 651 Td (A poisoned LEL sensor must not be recalibrated. If E-117 recurs within 30 days of replacement,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 638 Td (investigate the site for poisons such as silicone sealants, silicone-based lubricants or high) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 625 Td (H2S concentrations.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 600 Td (5. Replacing electrochemical sensors \(O2, CO, H2S\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 578 Td (1. Locate the sensor \(O2 top left, CO bottom left, H2S bottom right on the HX-210 and HX-220;) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 565 Td (   the HX-200 has a single central socket\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 552 Td (2. Pull the sensor straight out of its socket.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 539 Td (3. Remove the shorting spring from the new sensor, if fitted. CO and H2S sensors are shipped) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 526 Td (   with a shorting spring; O2 sensors are not.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 513 Td (4. Insert the new sensor with the locating tab facing the display.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 500 Td (5. Refit the rear housing with a new gasket. Tighten the screws to 0.45 N m \(HX-210 and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 487 Td (   HX-220\) or 0.35 N m \(HX-200\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 474 Td (6. Switch on and confirm "NEW SENSOR".) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 461 Td (7. Allow a warm-up period of 1 hour for CO and H2S sensors, or 30 minutes for the O2 sensor,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 448 Td (   before calibrating.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 435 Td (8. Calibrate all channels and perform a bump test.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 419 Td (6. Records and disposal) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 397 Td (Record the old and new sensor serial numbers in Meridian Link \(Instruments > [serial] > Service) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 384 Td (History\). Electrochemical sensors contain small amounts of acid electrolyte and lead \(O2\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 371 Td (Dispose of them as hazardous waste in accordance with local regulations. Sensors that fail) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 358 Td (within warranty should be kept for 30 days in case the warranty claim requires return.) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
